## ✅ Key Learning Outcomes

- Invite an individual external user as a guest in Entra ID
- Understand the B2B invitation flow and email delivery
- Download, complete, and upload the bulk invite CSV template
- Verify guest user accounts in the All Users list
- Identify guest vs member user types in the directory
- Understand Conditional Access policies for guest users
- Manage guest user resource assignments

---

## 🔑 Key Concepts for SC-300 Exam

| Concept | What to Know |
|---|---|
| B2B collaboration | External users invited as guests — use their own identity to access your resources |
| Guest user type | User type = Guest (vs Member for internal users) |
| Invitation flow | Invite sent by email → guest accepts → account active in directory |
| Guest Inviter role | Limited role that can only invite guests — cannot manage other users |
| Email restrictions | No group emails; no plus (+) symbols in email addresses |
| Bulk invite | CSV file with email address and redirection URL — uploaded via Bulk operations |
| Conditional Access | Can target guest users specifically with stricter policies |
| B2B vs B2C | B2B = partner/vendor collaboration; B2C = customer-facing identity |
| External collaboration settings | Controls who can invite guests and what guests can access |
